From: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 01:50:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: restart the radar detector after a full
 reset

A full reset loads the firmware again, which then knows nothing about
the radar detector, but the driver keeps the DFS state it had.  When
mac80211 sets the channel again, mt7996_dfs_init_radar_detector() sees
no state change and neither starts the detector nor ends the CAC.  On a
DFS channel, MT7990 then sends nothing, not even beacons, until the
interface is restarted.

Forget the DFS state on a full reset.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 mt7996/mac.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -2495,8 +2495,11 @@ mt7996_mac_full_reset(struct mt7996_dev *dev)
 	if (i == 10)
 		dev_err(dev->mt76.dev, "chip full reset failed\n");
 
-	mt7996_for_each_phy(dev, phy)
+	mt7996_for_each_phy(dev, phy) {
 		phy->omac_mask = 0;
+		/* the new firmware has to start the radar detector again */
+		phy->mt76->dfs_state = MT_DFS_STATE_UNKNOWN;
+	}
 	dev->mld_idx_mask = 0;
 	dev->mld_remap_idx_mask = 0;
 
